description:
Add a feature at the end of the history (or at the rollback marker) and regenerate. `kind` is easyCAD's feature JSON, one key naming the type. Examples:
{"Extrude":{"sketch":1,"profiles":"All","distance":"height","op":"NewBody"}}  (op: NewBody|Join|Cut|Intersect; optional symmetric, reverse, draft_deg, target {feature,index})
{"Revolve":{"sketch":2,"profiles":"All","axis":{"origin":[0,0,0],"dir":[0,0,1]},"angle_deg":"360","op":"Join"}}
{"Shell":{"open_faces":[{"Extreme":{"normal":[0,0,1],"which":"Max"}}],"thickness":"wall"}}
{"Fillet":{"edges":[{"Parallel":{"dir":[0,0,1]}}],"radius":"corner_r","auto_reduce":false}}
{"Chamfer":{"edges":[{"OfFace":{"Extreme":{"normal":[0,0,-1],"which":"Max"}}}],"distance":"0.5"}}
{"Draft":{"faces":[...],"neutral":{"origin":[0,0,0],"x_dir":[1,0,0],"normal":[0,0,1]},"pull":[0,0,1],"angle_deg":"1"}}
{"ScrewBoss":{"plane":{...},"points":[[10,10],[-10,10]],"od":"6","hole_dia":"2.5","height":"8"}}
Also Rib, Pattern, Mirror, Split, PartingJoint, InsertPart (see the easycad skill). Mesh bodies (from import_mesh) combine with solids:
{"MeshBoolean":{"target":{"feature":9,"index":0},"tools":[{"feature":2,"index":0}],"op":"Cut","clearance":"0.4","positions":[[0,0,0],[0,0,"stroke"]]}}  (op Join|Cut|Intersect; clearance grows tools for Cut, shrinks them for Intersect; positions = where the target travels, the tools are cleared at each; keep_tools default true)
{"TransformBody":{"body":{"feature":9,"index":0},"translate":[0,0,14],"rotate_deg":[0,0,90],"scale":"1","copy":true,"new_name":"Pile at B"}}  (move/rotate/copy any body; scale on mesh bodies only)
{"Split":{"body":{"feature":9,"index":0},"plane":{"origin":[0,0,0],"x_dir":[1,0,0],"normal":[0,0,1]},"offset":"2","new_name":"","keep":"Above"}}  (flat bottom; keep Both|Below|Above, works on mesh bodies)
Fillet, Chamfer, Shell, Draft, Rib, bosses and joints refuse mesh bodies; an Extrude Join/Cut with a mesh body as `target` works. Dimensions are expressions (strings) or numbers. Address faces and edges with selectors, never indices: faces {"Extreme":{normal,which:Max|Min}} (the outermost planar face facing `normal`), {"AllWithNormal":{normal}}, {"Cylinders":{radius,axis}}, {"Hint":{centroid,normal,kind}}; edges {"OfFace":<face>}, {"Between":[<face>,<face>]}, {"Parallel":{dir}}, {"Circles":{radius,near}}, {"Hint":{midpoint,tangent,kind}}. measure and get_selection return ready-made selectors. Omitted `body`/`target` means the last solid body (mesh bodies are used only when named). The reply has this feature's regen status (fillets: the summary with each failed edge's largest workable size) and the status of every feature after it. A feature that ends in error is taken back out (no undo step left behind) unless keep_on_error is true.
